2.3 Any hazard class not listed in Section 2.1 requires written approval from HPL Environment, Health & Safety (EHS) before it is booked.

## 3. Lithium Batteries

3.1 Lithium batteries are Class 9 dangerous goods. HPL recognizes the following UN numbers: {{ f.hazmat.lithium_un_numbers | join(", ") }}.

- UN3480 - lithium ion batteries shipped on their own.
- UN3481 - lithium ion batteries packed with or contained in equipment (for example laptops or headsets).
- UN3090 / UN3091 - lithium metal batteries, alone or with/in equipment.

3.2 Lithium battery shipments are treated as hazmat for carrier selection, dock booking and storage, including UN3481 batteries installed in equipment.

3.3 Packages must carry the Class 9 lithium battery hazard label or lithium battery mark, as applicable.

3.4 Damaged, defective or recalled lithium batteries are not accepted.

