## 5. Booking and Documentation

5.1 The customer must submit a Safety Data Sheet (SDS) for every hazmat SKU at least {{ f.hazmat.sds_required_hours_before }} hours before the first shipment or receipt.

5.2 Dock appointments for hazmat loads must be booked at least {{ f.dock_rules.hazmat_booking_lead_hours }} hours in advance and only at a designated hazmat dock:
{% for w in f.warehouses %}
- {{ w.code }}: {% if w.hazmat_docks %}dock{% if w.hazmat_docks|length > 1 %}s{% endif %} {{ w.hazmat_docks | join(" and ") }}{% else %}hazmat not accepted{% endif %}{% endfor %}

5.3 Every hazmat shipment must have shipping papers listing the UN number, proper shipping name, hazard class, packing group and quantity, plus 24-hour emergency response information.

5.4 A hazmat handling fee of {{ f.surcharges.hazmat_fee_usd | usd }} per shipment applies (HPL-LEG-001, Section 5.4).

## 6. Loading and Segregation

6.1 No more than {{ f.hazmat.max_hazmat_pallets_per_trailer }} hazmat pallets may be loaded on a single trailer.

6.2 Class 8 corrosives must not be loaded directly adjacent to Class 3 flammable liquids; separate them with non-hazmat freight or a load bar.

6.3 Hazmat pallets are loaded toward the rear of the trailer where possible, to allow quick access by emergency responders.

6.4 Placards are required when the aggregate gross weight of hazmat on a vehicle is 1,001 lb or more, and for any quantity where regulations require it.

## 7. Storage

7.1 Hazmat SKUs may only be stored at facilities with hazmat docks, in the designated hazmat storage area.

7.2 Flammable liquids (Class 3) are stored in fire-rated cabinets or a sprinklered flammable storage room.

7.3 Lithium battery stock is stored away from heat sources and separated from flammable liquids.

## 8. Incident Response

8.1 Any spill, leak or damaged hazmat package must be isolated immediately and reported to the facility supervisor.

8.2 The facility supervisor notifies HPL EHS within 1 hour of any hazmat incident, and the customer the same business day.

8.3 Only EHS-trained staff may clean up a spill, using the spill kit located at each hazmat dock.

## 9. Compliance and Violations

9.1 Tendering hazmat to a carrier that is not hazmat-certified is a **critical violation**. The shipment must be reported to EHS as soon as it is discovered, the customer informed, and the carrier relationship reviewed under HPL-LEG-001, Section 7.3.

9.2 EHS audits hazmat shipment records monthly, checking the carrier's certification, the dock used and the documentation for every hazmat shipment.

9.3 Staff who knowingly bypass this policy are subject to disciplinary action.
